# CTRL writes are discarded whole and the register keeps the firmware value.
# Measured on Damian's Intel I219-V, 2026-08-13, across two flights: the
# probe cleared CTRL.SLU and read it straight back and got 0x180240 every
# time. MDIC writes work on that same part, so this is CTRL specifically.
#
# -e1000-phy-link is on because the point of the arm is that the link comes
# up ANYWAY, over MDIO, with CTRL contributing nothing. Without it STATUS.LU
# would follow CTRL.SLU and the row would prove nothing.
-e1000-ctrl-ro
-e1000-phy-link